 r←CloneRepo(space folder args);branch;depth;repo;path;cmd;dry;name;isSSH;short
⍝ Clone a repository, by default from GitHub and into the current directory.
⍝ Desc: Creates a clone of the given repository
⍝ Parse: 2s -branch= -depth= -dry
⍝ Project: 0
 r←''
 'Right argument is invalid (empty)'Assert 0<≢args.Arguments
 branch←''args.Switch'branch'
 depth←args.Switch'depth'
 dry←args.Switch'dry'
 (repo path)←args.(_1 _2)
 'First arguement is invalid (no "/"separating group and repo-name)'Assert'/'∊repo
 :If isSSH←'@'∊repo
     :If short←'@'=1⍴repo
         repo←'git@github.com:',1↓repo
     :EndIf
     'Invalid SSH address'Assert'git@'{⍺≡(≢⍺)↑⍵}repo
 :ElseIf ∧/'http://' 'https://'{⍺≢(≢⍺)↑⍵}¨⊂repo
     repo←'https://github.com/',repo
 :EndIf
 :If isSSH
 :AndIf short∨∨/'github.com'⍷repo   ⍝ Short syntax default to GitHub
     :If {0=⎕NC ⍵:1 ⋄ ~⍎⍵}'∆SSH_OK'
         ∆SSH_OK←##.GitHub_SSH_OK
     :EndIf
     'Cannot access GitHub via SSH'Assert ∆SSH_OK
 :EndIf
 repo,←('.git'{⍺≢(-≢⍺)↑⍵}repo)/'.git'
 name←⊃⊣/'.'(≠⊆⊢)⊃(⊢/'/'(≠⊆⊢)repo)
 :If 0≡path
     path←##.F.EnforceSlash ##.F.PWD,'/',name
 :AndIf ~dry
     :If 0=##.CommTools.YesOrNo'Sure you want to clone into ',path,' ?'
         r←'Cancelled by user' ⋄ →0
     :EndIf
 :Else
     path←##.F.EnforceSlash path
     :If name≢⊃⊢/'/'(≠⊆⊢)path
         path,←'/',name
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 :If ⎕NEXISTS path
     ('Not empty: ',path)Assert 0=≢⊃##.F.Dir path,'/*'
 :Else
     ⎕MKDIR path
 :EndIf
 r←dry ##.CloneRepo repo path branch depth
 :If dry
     r←'git ',r
 :EndIf
 ⍝Done
